es[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]webkind: delete MemoryWeb.rendering_type, stop reading type:/parent: [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from web descriptors, strip both keys on init, always inline every web [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]descriptor, and update every consumer surface that displayed a web's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rendering tier.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Tier-free H2 sections and the new Memory Webs section[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]section[dim] · [dim][/dim]after webkind[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: rename the generated H2 anchors to Core Memory / Memory Webs / [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Reference Memory, rename the AGENTS template variables, render web [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]descriptors into the new middle section, and teach the AGENTS.md parser [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and TUI rail the three-group shape.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation, memory notes, and regenerated artifacts[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after section[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: rewrite the tier vocabulary in docs/, the generated sase.md and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]README memory templates, the affected glossary strands, and a new [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]decision record, then regenerate and commit every generated artifact [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]here and in the chezmoi linked repo.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-vk","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-vk.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-f740e24843850288076a72f4b8e0468c","started_at":"2026-08-29T15:31:00.213040+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-vk",